WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.900
The F1 score.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.100
What if you need a single number that respects both precision and recall?

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.467
F1 is the harmonic mean of precision and recall.

4
00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.733
Harmonic, not arithmetic, and that choice has teeth.

5
00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:19.267
It is dragged toward the smaller value, so you cannot max one metric and abandon the other.

6
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.700
Here is the formula.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.933
Two times precision times recall, over precision plus recall.

8
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:30.467
F1 is one only when both are one, and zero if either is zero.

9
00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.167
Watch what happens with an imbalanced model.

10
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.859
Precision is point nine, but recall is only point three.

11
00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:41.433
The simple average says sixty percent, which is flattering.

12
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:43.564
F1 says forty five percent.

13
00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:45.667
It punishes the imbalance hard.

14
00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:48.267
The same thing in Python.

15
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.100
We compute F1 from precision and recall.

16
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.782
The plain average gives point six.

17
00:00:53.782 --> 00:00:55.533
F1 gives point four five.

18
00:00:56.733 --> 00:01:00.933
In an experiment tracker, F1 gives the leaderboard one honest column.

19
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:07.733
The forest has precision point eight eight but recall only point six one, so F1 is point seven two.

20
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.933
XGBoost is balanced, and scores point eight.

21
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:13.833
Simple averaging would call it nearly a tie.

22
00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.433
A few variants exist.

23
00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:20.700
Use F1 to compare models with one number on imbalanced data.

24
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.400
F zero point five weights precision more.

25
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.362
And F2 weights recall more.

26
00:01:25.362 --> 00:01:28.500
If error costs differ a lot, read the pair instead.

27
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.513
Let's recap.

28
00:01:30.513 --> 00:01:33.767
F1 is the harmonic mean of precision and recall.

29
00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.933
It sinks toward the weaker of the two.

30
00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:38.933
So imbalance is punished, not averaged away.

31
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:41.300
Next up: ROC AUC.
